I found another decent way to rid oneself of the hack virus: decide you
want to compile your own version, with new monsters and stuff...

Ok I started on my quest to make my own improvements to Hack one day and
realised that without a C compilor I was pretty screwed from the outset so
I decided to download the djgpp version, since it's free. Ok so here I am
running at 1200 baud, cause that's what the uplink I'm using to get to
internet runs at, trying to get the several megs of stuff. Well there's
some garbage on the line so I can only run it for an hour at a time
successfully. (Not to mention my parents need the phone a lot) So 10 or 15
days later I finally have a compilor. I try it with the samples inclosed.
It dies and starts writing garbage all over the place. With very little
damage to my drive, sigh of relief, I delete everything and try again with
a newer version I just found. 10 days later I have it. Yeah! It worked.

Now I had to get the 3 megs of Hack source. Another several days.

Found out I need ndmake as opposed to gnumake. Another day.

Found out I really needed flex and bison after all, another day.

Ok a month later I sit down in front of my computer and type make, it
works. I hadn't looked at the source code yet. I look at the source code.
I shudder. Me thinks it will be a while afore the Iverson Improvements
(very similar to some things Tim Allen might do) are found out there on
the net.

Gimme another month, I'll have my own version of '--' out there...

Wish me luck...

